1
00:00:02,767 --> 00:00:04,673
Hey.

2
00:00:04,673 --> 00:00:06,273
Hey.

3
00:00:06,273 --> 00:00:08,991
- Sorry, I know you're busy.
- It's fine.

4
00:00:09,614 --> 00:00:14,041
Man, your leaving the project so suddenly
came as a huge shock.

5
00:00:15,303 --> 00:00:18,447
It was fun working together,
the three of us.

6
00:00:24,044 --> 00:00:25,704
What did you need?

7
00:00:28,514 --> 00:00:30,512
Are things going well...

8
00:00:31,516 --> 00:00:33,165
with Yamane?

9
00:00:34,061 --> 00:00:35,268
Huh?

10
00:00:37,246 --> 00:00:39,348
It's none of my business, right?

11
00:00:40,038 --> 00:00:41,343
Sorry.

12
00:00:42,433 --> 00:00:45,655
But I'm just worried.

13
00:00:50,509 --> 00:00:52,309
It doesn't involve you.

14
00:00:54,930 --> 00:00:56,881
What if I said it does?

15
00:01:01,937 --> 00:01:03,824
I'm kidding.

16
00:01:12,296 --> 00:01:13,744
You know...

17
00:01:18,474 --> 00:01:21,522
I was jealous of you in high school.

18
00:01:21,522 --> 00:01:22,763
Huh?

19
00:01:24,315 --> 00:01:29,895
You can get along with anyone, unlike me.

20
00:01:30,825 --> 00:01:33,601
You could handle everything so well.

21
00:01:35,935 --> 00:01:37,336
What?

22
00:01:38,661 --> 00:01:42,918
I never thought you'd feel that way.

23
00:01:49,963 --> 00:01:52,571
Maybe I was jealous too.

24
00:01:54,039 --> 00:01:55,212
Huh?

25
00:01:56,059 --> 00:02:02,303
Yamane always smiles so naturally
when she's with you.

26
00:02:03,534 --> 00:02:06,528
But she never makes that face with me.

27
00:02:12,174 --> 00:02:13,854
So...

28
00:02:14,751 --> 00:02:18,448
you two have to be happy.
Or else it'll bother me.

29
00:02:26,775 --> 00:02:28,315
I know.

30
00:02:32,512 --> 00:02:34,152
Really?

31
00:02:36,418 --> 00:02:38,161
I was surprised when you asked me here.

32
00:02:38,161 --> 00:02:40,272
It's fine, isn't it?

33
00:03:32,816 --> 00:03:36,773
There. Silky, smooth hair.

34
00:03:39,045 --> 00:03:41,098
Feel a bit better now?

35
00:03:46,727 --> 00:03:49,497
You're amazing, Nagi.

36
00:03:51,493 --> 00:03:56,481
You are so good at picking up
on people's feelings.

37
00:03:59,788 --> 00:04:01,654
Taguchi...

38
00:04:04,912 --> 00:04:07,188
transferred schools.

39
00:04:09,924 --> 00:04:11,452
That's so sudden.

40
00:04:16,739 --> 00:04:21,146
He didn't say anything,
and I can't get in touch with him.

41
00:04:26,425 --> 00:04:28,335
Did I...

42
00:04:29,898 --> 00:04:33,060
do something to make him hate me?

43
00:04:43,118 --> 00:04:45,816
But your stories about him were always fun.

44
00:04:47,308 --> 00:04:49,924
Like eating lunch together.

45
00:04:50,865 --> 00:04:52,932
Or going to festivals.

46
00:04:57,589 --> 00:05:00,100
Maybe you can have faith.

47
00:05:00,884 --> 00:05:03,337
Believe in the Taguchi that you know.

48
00:05:07,848 --> 00:05:10,682
Maybe you can try trusting in...

49
00:05:13,003 --> 00:05:15,067
your relationship together.

50
00:05:25,561 --> 00:05:28,371
Visiting the school tomorrow?

51
00:05:29,893 --> 00:05:31,224
Yes.

52
00:05:31,831 --> 00:05:34,248
Have fun.

53
00:05:34,248 --> 00:05:37,022
I'll be waiting to hear about it.

54
00:05:43,637 --> 00:05:45,119
Actually...

55
00:05:47,001 --> 00:05:52,048
Could we talk about other things
besides that too?

56
00:05:56,814 --> 00:05:58,214
Of course.

57
00:06:03,217 --> 00:06:06,558
[Tsurushiro High School]
Huh? Did I say that?

58
00:06:06,558 --> 00:06:08,064
You did.

59
00:06:08,064 --> 00:06:14,095
You said, "I learned about a cappella
and drinking parties in college!"

60
00:06:14,095 --> 00:06:18,952
Did I? I don't remember that at all.

61
00:06:18,952 --> 00:06:20,918
I'll go buy some drinks.

62
00:06:20,918 --> 00:06:23,064
Oh, there's some in the staff room.

63
00:06:23,064 --> 00:06:24,570
It's totally fine.

64
00:06:25,928 --> 00:06:27,394
That brings back memories.

65
00:06:27,394 --> 00:06:29,149
- A cappella, right?
- Yeah.

66
00:06:29,149 --> 00:06:30,937
- Me?
- Yes.

67
00:07:00,810 --> 00:07:02,223
Sorry for the wait.

68
00:07:02,223 --> 00:07:03,943
You took forever.

69
00:07:03,943 --> 00:07:07,503
I've been wanting to give this to you,
Yamane.

70
00:07:15,540 --> 00:07:17,233
This is...

71
00:07:17,233 --> 00:07:20,604
It's Taguchi's. He transferred, right?

72
00:07:20,604 --> 00:07:23,643
Felt wrong to just throw it out.

73
00:07:23,643 --> 00:07:25,653
You two were close, right?

74
00:07:25,653 --> 00:07:27,811
Do you still keep in touch?

75
00:07:27,811 --> 00:07:29,924
I want you to give this back.

76
00:07:32,318 --> 00:07:33,698
Sure.

77
00:07:33,698 --> 00:07:35,585
That helps me out.

78
00:07:36,290 --> 00:07:39,036
Man, which restaurant should we go to?

79
00:07:39,036 --> 00:07:41,139
I'm not sure.

80
00:07:41,139 --> 00:07:43,857
Do you prefer meat or fish?

81
00:07:43,857 --> 00:07:44,923
Meat, I guess?

82
00:07:44,923 --> 00:07:46,586
Meat it is.
[Ryosuke Taguchi: Let's talk in person.]

83
00:07:46,586 --> 00:07:49,876
Was there a BBQ place near the station?
[Ryosuke Taguchi: Let's talk in person.]

84
00:07:55,668 --> 00:07:57,260
Ms. Yamane, sorry.

85
00:07:57,260 --> 00:08:00,425
Can I go drinking with the teacher alone?

86
00:08:00,425 --> 00:08:01,425
Huh?

87
00:08:01,425 --> 00:08:05,568
There's something I really need
to discuss with him one-on-one.

88
00:08:05,568 --> 00:08:07,672
- Is that so?
- Yes.

89
00:08:09,042 --> 00:08:10,685
Sorry, Ms. Yamane.

90
00:08:10,685 --> 00:08:13,346
You can go home now.

91
00:08:22,836 --> 00:08:24,064
Okay.

92
00:08:25,617 --> 00:08:27,030
I'll be going first.

93
00:08:27,030 --> 00:08:29,904
- Thanks.
- Thank you.

94
00:08:30,563 --> 00:08:31,930
Do you drink a lot?

95
00:08:31,930 --> 00:08:35,672
Well, my tolerance has gotten a lot weaker.

96
00:08:40,454 --> 00:08:42,121
<i>Hello?</i>

97
00:08:43,562 --> 00:08:45,549
Sorry to bother you.

98
00:08:47,073 --> 00:08:48,406
<i>It's fine.</i>

99
00:08:50,948 --> 00:08:52,577
Actually...

100
00:08:55,961 --> 00:08:57,955
Can we meet now?

101
00:09:04,137 --> 00:09:05,445
<i>Yeah.</i>

102
00:09:07,370 --> 00:09:09,158
<i>I want to see you too.</i>

103
00:09:12,956 --> 00:09:14,803
Where are you now?

104
00:09:18,193 --> 00:09:22,817
<i>That place we went to
after sneaking out of school.</i>

105
00:09:33,606 --> 00:09:35,299
Ryosuke!

106
00:09:52,699 --> 00:09:56,531
How was school?

107
00:09:58,851 --> 00:10:00,044
Huh?

108
00:10:00,959 --> 00:10:02,696
Like, the teacher.

109
00:10:03,787 --> 00:10:05,281
How was he?

110
00:10:11,445 --> 00:10:13,386
He seemed well.

111
00:10:15,897 --> 00:10:17,237
I see.

112
00:10:34,104 --> 00:10:35,592
Sorry.

113
00:10:36,264 --> 00:10:37,745
You see...

114
00:10:42,394 --> 00:10:46,961
Where... do I even start?

115
00:10:50,627 --> 00:10:54,837
I really should have thought it through more.

116
00:11:14,436 --> 00:11:16,322
Can I tell you...

117
00:11:19,307 --> 00:11:21,091
what happened?

118
00:11:25,456 --> 00:11:26,634
Yeah.

119
00:11:37,573 --> 00:11:39,603
In middle school,

120
00:11:41,449 --> 00:11:43,682
my parents got divorced.

121
00:11:44,797 --> 00:11:46,090
What?

122
00:11:47,769 --> 00:11:54,858
Well, that itself wasn't that big of a deal
to me.

123
00:11:59,478 --> 00:12:01,126
But back then...

124
00:12:03,218 --> 00:12:07,032
I was just irrationally angry
about everything.

125
00:12:10,606 --> 00:12:12,320
And so...

126
00:12:13,707 --> 00:12:15,749
That's how I ended up.

127
00:12:16,787 --> 00:12:18,815
But...

128
00:12:18,815 --> 00:12:23,241
I think they suit you. They look nice.

129
00:12:24,481 --> 00:12:27,265
<i>That's when I met you, Shiori.</i>

130
00:12:28,618 --> 00:12:31,164
And before I knew it, I was in love.

131
00:12:36,317 --> 00:12:38,867
Yamane plays around, huh?

132
00:12:38,867 --> 00:12:40,782
Then... maybe I have a shot.

133
00:12:40,782 --> 00:12:41,967
- I think so!
- Really?

134
00:12:41,967 --> 00:12:44,939
- Yeah!
- Man, maybe I'll go for it.

135
00:12:44,939 --> 00:12:46,166
Hey!

136
00:12:49,098 --> 00:12:51,131
What'd you say just now?

137
00:12:51,843 --> 00:12:54,123
I'm just kidding, come on.

138
00:12:56,590 --> 00:12:58,856
What?

139
00:12:58,856 --> 00:13:00,312
I'm not serious...

140
00:13:00,312 --> 00:13:02,953
Listen up, punks.

141
00:13:03,795 --> 00:13:05,553
If you lay a finger on her...

142
00:13:05,553 --> 00:13:07,133
Taguchi.

143
00:13:12,209 --> 00:13:13,809
What's wrong?

144
00:13:17,438 --> 00:13:20,665
- Let's go...
- Hey! What are you guys doing?

145
00:13:23,492 --> 00:13:25,958
<i>I wanted to protect you.</i>

146
00:13:28,462 --> 00:13:30,788
So I left without telling you.

147
00:13:37,608 --> 00:13:41,362
I hated how that was
the only way I could react.

148
00:13:45,909 --> 00:13:51,064
So I dyed my hair black
and stopped wearing earrings.

149
00:13:55,485 --> 00:13:57,459
And then...

150
00:14:02,354 --> 00:14:07,447
people started gathering around me.

151
00:14:16,347 --> 00:14:18,061
And I realized...

152
00:14:19,560 --> 00:14:22,383
that's all it takes.

153
00:14:32,256 --> 00:14:34,667
Even though I pushed you away...

154
00:14:40,277 --> 00:14:42,945
I kept wishing you were here.

155
00:15:01,429 --> 00:15:02,844
Hey...

156
00:15:05,474 --> 00:15:06,834
These...

157
00:15:10,119 --> 00:15:14,689
They're something you held dear.

158
00:15:18,971 --> 00:15:20,823
Can I put them on you?

159
00:15:53,893 --> 00:15:56,178
About back then...

160
00:15:57,837 --> 00:16:00,202
To me,

161
00:16:01,214 --> 00:16:05,097
every bit of it is a wonderful memory.

162
00:16:18,021 --> 00:16:20,824
When you transferred,

163
00:16:24,993 --> 00:16:27,160
it surprised me.

164
00:16:30,692 --> 00:16:33,107
When you were gone...

165
00:16:35,032 --> 00:16:37,464
I missed you, but...

166
00:16:40,626 --> 00:16:47,238
The time we spent together
was always shining in my mind.

167
00:16:53,664 --> 00:17:00,025
Do you remember how you told me
I can easily make other friends?

168
00:17:05,261 --> 00:17:07,315
There weren't many,

169
00:17:08,014 --> 00:17:11,638
but I really did make friends.

170
00:17:15,287 --> 00:17:17,257
You gave me courage,

171
00:17:19,542 --> 00:17:21,503
and I'm really grateful.

172
00:17:24,659 --> 00:17:26,191
You really...

173
00:17:28,966 --> 00:17:30,903
haven't changed, have you?

174
00:17:41,449 --> 00:17:42,978
I'm sorry.

175
00:17:45,074 --> 00:17:46,442
I'm...

176
00:17:47,620 --> 00:17:49,784
so pathetic.

177
00:17:53,653 --> 00:17:56,167
It's okay to show that side of you.

178
00:18:01,602 --> 00:18:04,196
Since it's you, Ryosuke.

179
00:18:06,449 --> 00:18:08,496
You can share everything.

180
00:18:41,897 --> 00:18:43,798
I'm so glad

181
00:18:46,438 --> 00:18:48,391
we got to meet again.

182
00:18:53,418 --> 00:18:55,188
Me too.

183
00:19:39,359 --> 00:19:40,735
Hey...

184
00:19:42,808 --> 00:19:44,596
You're Yamane, right?

185
00:19:47,103 --> 00:19:49,064
Yes, that's me.

186
00:19:50,906 --> 00:19:52,587
Do you remember me?

187
00:19:53,919 --> 00:19:55,846
It's me. Taguchi.

188
00:20:49,120 --> 00:20:50,299
Huh?

189
00:20:51,460 --> 00:20:53,153
Were you awake?

190
00:20:54,381 --> 00:20:55,889
No.

191
00:20:58,550 --> 00:21:00,774
I'm not awake.

192
00:21:02,325 --> 00:21:04,376
You are.

193
00:21:04,376 --> 00:21:07,930
<i>Those days when everything seemed to shine</i>

194
00:21:07,930 --> 00:21:09,617
<i>have come back more vividly.</i>

195
00:21:09,617 --> 00:21:12,690
- No.
- Kiss me again.

196
00:21:12,690 --> 00:21:15,841
<i>Right now, being close to you...</i>

197
00:21:15,841 --> 00:21:17,400
- No.
- The other side.

198
00:21:17,400 --> 00:21:19,313
<i>...is happiness.</i>

199
00:21:19,313 --> 00:21:22,697
I'm really glad that Taguchi came back.

200
00:21:22,697 --> 00:21:26,420
No, I didn't come back. I'm just helping out.

201
00:21:26,420 --> 00:21:30,568
But I was hoping we could go together,
so I'm happy.

202
00:21:31,162 --> 00:21:32,831
Yeah.

203
00:21:32,831 --> 00:21:36,189
Huh? I'm here too, you know.

204
00:21:37,366 --> 00:21:38,873
Let's go, Shiori.

205
00:21:39,459 --> 00:21:42,679
Huh? T-Taguchi?

206
00:21:43,533 --> 00:21:45,696
It's been a while.

207
00:21:45,696 --> 00:21:47,930
Ear... ring!

208
00:21:48,809 --> 00:21:50,944
Hey, I'm not even wearing any.

209
00:21:52,163 --> 00:21:56,655
Also, what a crazy miracle
that you're all working together.

210
00:21:56,655 --> 00:21:59,136
<i>- That's why...</i>
- Right?

211
00:21:59,136 --> 00:22:01,219
<i>From now on...</i>

212
00:22:02,232 --> 00:22:04,294
<i>Forever...</i>

213
00:22:05,418 --> 00:22:06,878
Huh?

214
00:22:10,953 --> 00:22:12,566
What's wrong?

215
00:22:13,771 --> 00:22:16,113
No, it's nothing.

216
00:22:44,645 --> 00:22:48,296
Brings back memories, huh?

217
00:22:50,058 --> 00:22:52,065
Yeah, it does.

218
00:22:57,939 --> 00:23:00,165
I want ice cream.

219
00:23:03,342 --> 00:23:05,389
Sneaking out again?

220
00:23:07,863 --> 00:23:10,220
No, I won't.

221
00:23:10,220 --> 00:23:11,727
I see.

222
00:23:16,001 --> 00:23:18,096
Did you want to?

223
00:23:19,066 --> 00:23:20,668
- A little.
- A little?

224
00:23:20,668 --> 00:23:21,981
A little.

225
00:23:22,846 --> 00:23:23,967
I see.

226
00:23:23,967 --> 00:23:28,808
Yeah. But I'm an adult now.

227
00:23:28,808 --> 00:23:30,575
I see.
